<div class="content">
  <h1 style="margin-top: 4rem; margin-bottom: 1rem;">Migrate from the legacy Zarr proxy</h1>

  <p>
    <strong><code>data.dynamical.org</code> stops serving legacy Zarr datasets after {{ legacyZarrMigration.sunsetDisplay }}.</strong>
    The datasets remain public and continue updating as Icechunk repositories.
  </p>
  <p>
    Replace each hard-coded <code>https://data.dynamical.org/.../latest.zarr</code>
    URL with one of the catalog-driven access patterns below. Both resolve the
    current repository from our <a href="https://stac.dynamical.org/catalog.json">STAC catalog</a>,
    so your code does not need to track storage locations or version changes.
  </p>

  <h2>Recommended: dynamical-catalog</h2>
  <p>
    Use Python 3.12 or newer and install <code>dynamical-catalog&gt;=0.7.0</code>.
    Pass the replacement dataset ID from the table below.
  </p>
  <pre><code class="language-python">import dynamical_catalog

ds = dynamical_catalog.open("noaa-gfs-forecast", chunks=None)</code></pre>

  <h2>Direct STAC and Icechunk</h2>
  <p>
    Resolve the <code>icechunk-https</code> asset from STAC each time your
    application opens a repository. Do not copy and permanently hard-code the
    asset URL.
  </p>
  <pre><code class="language-python">import icechunk
import pystac
import xarray as xr

catalog = pystac.Catalog.from_file("https://stac.dynamical.org/catalog.json")
collection = catalog.get_child("noaa-gfs-forecast")
asset = collection.assets["icechunk-https"]

repo = icechunk.Repository.open(icechunk.http_storage(asset.href))
session = repo.readonly_session("main")
ds = xr.open_zarr(session.store, consolidated=False, chunks=None)</code></pre>

  <h2>Legacy URL mapping</h2>
  <div class="table-container">
    <table class="data">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Legacy path</th>
          <th>Replacement dataset ID</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {% for route in legacyZarrMigration.routes %}
          <tr>
            <td><code>data.dynamical.org{{ route.legacyPath }}/latest.zarr</code></td>
            <td>
              <a href="/catalog/{{ route.datasetId }}/"><code>{{ route.datasetId }}</code></a>
              · <a href="https://stac.dynamical.org/{{ route.datasetId }}/collection.json">STAC</a>
              {% if route.note %}<br><small>{{ route.note }}</small>{% endif %}
            </td>
          </tr>
        {% endfor %}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2>What changes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Opening requires Icechunk 2 and Python 3.12 or newer.</li>
    <li>The public STAC Collection is the source of truth for the current repository.</li>
    <li>Dataset IDs replace legacy proxy paths; dimensions and variable coverage are documented on each catalog page.</li>
    <li>The optional <code>?email=</code> query argument is no longer used.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Help</h2>
  <p>
    If the replacement does not cover your access pattern, email
    <a href="mailto:feedback@dynamical.org">feedback@dynamical.org</a> with the
    legacy URL, variables, spatial subset, and time range you use.
  </p>
</div>
